studio-1810c (1.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The window fits the screen it opens on (1024x680 minimum): 1400x880 on a
    1366x768 laptop pushed the master faders off the bottom.
  * Channel strips shrink below 1500 px so more fit on a laptop, and their
    names no longer truncate to "Analo...".
  * Meters re-read the node channel count when the stream restarts, so an
    ALTSET change cannot leave the bars reading the wrong channels.
  * A Studio 1824 or 1824c is refused by name instead of a generic "no device":
    their matrix is a different size and nothing is written to them.
  * `uc1810c.py doctor` reports the meter sources, which is the first thing to
    check when bars are missing.
  * Packaging: RPM built on Fedora 40 and rpmlint-clean (0 errors, 0 warnings,
    exceptions declared with reasons); PKGBUILD checksum is real, not SKIP.
  * CI runs the protocol, meter and device-guard tests and fails on any lintian
    output.

 -- Studio 1810c for Linux <studio-1810c@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:10:00 +0100

studio-1810c (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Level meters for every input strip and output pair, computed from the audio
    stream through PipeWire (the device reports no levels - see PROTOCOL.md).
  * Poll the state packet at 2 Hz instead of faster: the device stalls 0xA1 with
    EPIPE above roughly 4 Hz while streaming.
  * Reconnect to the interface if it is plugged in after the window opened.

 -- Studio 1810c for Linux <studio-1810c@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:30:00 +0100

studio-1810c (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release.
  * Vendor USB protocol implemented from the macOS Universal Control 5.1.1
    binaries: 18x10 routing matrix, output faders, front-panel switches,
    clock status.
  * GTK3 + WebKit2 desktop window following the Universal Control layout.
  * udev rule shipped by the package, so no manual permission step.

 -- Studio 1810c for Linux <studio-1810c@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
